{
  "rationale": "The plant G models the robot's perception and motion event possibilities, including all five controllable actions and all four uncontrollable sensor events. States encode the robot's current square side (1-4), corner, and recovery/commit phases. The specification E constrains the robot to follow the square path, only using move_backward in dedicated front-obstacle recovery states, and ensures recovery is brief and directed. Obstacle handling is conservative but returns to the square sequence as soon as path_clear is observed.",
  "strategy": [
    "Explicitly encode square path progress (side1, side2, side3, side4) and corners, so the robot resumes the correct sequence after recovery.",
    "Obstacle recovery uses short directed turns or, if repeatedly blocked, a last-resort full_rotate. move_backward is only allowed from a dedicated recover_back state after obstacle_front. After any recovery, the robot returns to the square sequence at the correct side."
  ],
